SLoTH Results Summary (2026-04-12)
Method
SLoTH (Single-Loop Training with Hard constraints) replaces PINet's two-loop adjoint system (4000 matrix-vector products in the backward pass) with a warm-started first-order momentum solver on the normal equations of the IFT adjoint system.

Adjoint system
(I - J_s^T) v = c_s
where c_s = step_final^T · ∇_z L.

SLoTH solver variants
SLoTH-HB (Heavy-Ball): Fixed step size

v_{k+1} = v_k - α·∇f(v_k) + β·(v_k - v_{k-1})
SLoTH-CA (Cosine-Annealed): Step size decays within inner solve

α_i = α_min + 0.5·(α_max - α_min)·(1 + cos(πi/k))
SLoTH-RM (Recursive Momentum): Variance-reduced recursive gradient

d_k = ∇f(v_k) + (1 - β)·(d_{k-1} - ∇f(v_{k-1}))
v_{k+1} = v_k - α·d_k
SLoTH-CARM (Cosine-Annealed Recursive Momentum): Combines CA and RM

d_k = ∇f(v_k) + (1 - β)·(d_{k-1} - ∇f(v_{k-1}))
v_{k+1} = v_k - α_i·d_k   where α_i follows cosine schedule
All variants use:

Per-sample warm-start: v_0 from previous epoch's solution
Fixed β = 0.9 (momentum coefficient)
α (step size) and k (iterations) as tunable parameters
Matvec cost per backward pass
PINet: 4000 matvecs
SLoTH: 10-200 matvecs (k=5-100 iterations × 2 matvecs each)
